meta {
  name: Add Calendar Days (Custom range)
  type: http
  seq: 8
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/hr/calendar/days
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{hrAdminAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "source": "import",
    "days": [
      { "date": "2031-12-29", "kind": "holiday", "label": "Winter closure" },
      { "date": "2031-12-30", "kind": "holiday", "label": "Winter closure" },
      { "date": "2031-12-31", "kind": "holiday", "label": "Winter closure" },
      { "date": "2032-01-01", "kind": "holiday", "label": "Winter closure" },
      { "date": "2032-01-02", "kind": "holiday", "label": "Winter closure" }
    ]
  }
}

tests {
  test("returns 201 Created", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(201);
  });

  test("writes one row per working day, across the year boundary", function () {
    const days = res.getBody().days;
    expect(days.map((d) => d.date)).to.deep.equal([
      "2031-12-29", "2031-12-30", "2031-12-31", "2032-01-01", "2032-01-02",
    ]);
    expect(days.every((d) => d.label === "Winter closure")).to.equal(true);
    expect(days.every((d) => d.source === "import")).to.equal(true);
  });
}

docs {
  # POST /hr/calendar/days — a custom holiday range, as the web sends it (PAC-161 v2)

  - **Module:** `hr` · **Permission:** `agency:hr:admin`

  The holiday picker's "Custom holidays" section takes a name, a start and an
  end date. The API has no range shape: the **client** expands the range to
  one `holiday` row per day of the agency workweek (`expandHolidayRange` in
  `@sfa/shared`) and sends the rows in the same batch as the ticked
  suggestions, under the batch's `source` (`onboarding` from the setup step,
  `import` from the settings dialog). This body is "Winter closure,
  Dec 27 2031 – Jan 2 2032" on a Mon–Fri workweek: Dec 27–28 (a weekend) are
  skipped, the five weekdays are sent.

  Rules the client enforces before sending: end ≥ start, at most 60 days, the
  range starts in the shown year (it may run into the next one — a Christmas
  closure does), and no day collides with a ticked suggestion or a row
  already on the calendar (the API would answer `409` for the latter).

  ⚠ Re-running this request against the same database is a `409`: the dates
  are already active. Remove them through **Remove Calendar Day** or pick
  another year.

  ## Response `201` — `{ "days": [AgencyCalendarDayView…] }`, sorted by date.
}
